# Texas Hold’em

Physical cards stay offline. No shuffling, dealing, digital deck, or automatic hand evaluation. Optional community/hole-card records are display-only and never advance a street or settle a pot.

## Phase sequence

`POKER_SETUP → PRE_FLOP → FLOP → TURN → RIVER → SHOWDOWN → HAND_COMPLETE → PRE_FLOP`

Owner advances physical-card streets only after the betting round is matched. Blinds post automatically once per hand. One remaining Player awards the pot without Showdown and clears actor / to-call / waiting. If everyone remaining is All-In, Owner still deals remaining streets then Showdown. Next hand rotates the button once and posts blinds once.

## Distinct roles

- **Table Owner** (`isOwner`): table management and street buttons — never the rotating Button chrome
- **Dealer/Button** (`seat.isDealer`): rotating seated Player; posts blinds; acts normally; no Owner street controls
- **Current actor**: only seat that may Fold / Check or Call / Bet or Raise / All-In
- Others see whose turn it is; Folded/All-In keep seat status + wallet without tray actions

`pokerControls()` is the UI acceptance contract. Clients follow snapshot/SSE.

## Legal action matrix (summary)

| Phase | Owner (not acting) | Current actor | Others |
|---|---|---|---|
| POKER_SETUP | START HAND; menu invite/jetons/switch | — | Felt + wallet |
| PRE_FLOP…RIVER | Street button disabled until matched, then enabled | Actor actions + tray | Felt + whose turn + wallet |
| SHOWDOWN | AWARD POT | No actor actions | Results + wallet |
| HAND_COMPLETE | NEXT HAND | Wallet + result | Wallet + result |

- CALL stays available when chips are owed; never show `CALL 0` or `TO CALL 0`
- CHECK never while `toCall > 0`
- BET/RAISE opens a local composer; tray taps/drags stage only; CONFIRM commits once via existing `pokerAct` (idempotent)
- Stale actions return `TURN_CONFLICT` and refresh

## Canonical Tabletop surface

- **Visual authority:** `design/reference/tabletop/approved/poker-premium-racetrack.png` — literal composition/materials (leather rail, wood racetrack, forest felt, seat avatars+ledgers, centre pot, in-felt round track). Supersedes prior Poker mockups and flat-oval Tabletop styling.
- Shared `PokerBoard` via `PokerDealer` / `PokerPlayer` for **all** phases including Phase 0 — one active render path only
- `selectTableBoard` → `POKER_DEALER` / `POKER_PLAYER` at `POKER_SETUP` / table setup — never the Blackjack PhaseZero ledger
- Product state wins over mock: legal actions, offline cards (never render), factual names/balances, initials when no avatar, tray below table, responsive fit over room scenery
- FAIL: flat CSS oval; thin yellow outline rail; pill/card seats; round track outside felt; duplicated phase title; table name vs pot competition; digital cards; list layout; invented portraits; Classic CSS
- Inward street-wager chip stacks; **never** visible `STREET N` labels
- Centre pot shows committed total; side-pot lines only when side pots exist
- After HAND_COMPLETE: `POT PAID` / winners — no lingering TO CALL, actor, or Waiting seat
- Owner street controls in the phase dock, separated from actor actions above the tray
- Pulsing actor outline; `prefers-reduced-motion` uses a static strong outline
- Phase copy: one primary label + optional instruction (`phase-copy.ts`)
- START HAND stays pressable; server `POKER_SEATS` stays authoritative; map failures to one compact dock hint

## Owner buy-in (before a live hand)

- Reuse existing `giveJetons` → `distributeJetons` (ledger `BANK_DISTRIBUTION` / `INITIAL_ALLOCATION`) — no second funding path
- **Owner only** (`canGiveJetons`); Dealer-not-Owner and Players are rejected
- Available only during `POKER_SETUP` and `HAND_COMPLETE` (between hands); never while a hand has cards, actions, or a live pot
- Compact `BUY-IN` dock/menu control opens the existing player+amount sheet; refresh shows the new AVAILABLE balance

## Accounting reminders

- AVAILABLE → LOCKED_POKER only; no Bank reserve path for Poker wagers
- Side pots by all-in levels; equal splits with remainder left of button
- Game change closes the session and opens a fresh allocation — no leftover AVAILABLE into Poker
- New-session first deal requires a seated funded Poker Dealer (`assertFundedPokerDealer` when `sessionStarting`)
